nThus, discard **W5** is reasonable.  \\n\\n**Reason:**  \\nWe need to discard one tile after claiming Chi. Keeping the pair B5 is essential for a quick win. Keeping the complete T5,T6,T7 chow gives one ready meld. W6,W7 can form a chow with W5 or W8, giving a two-sided wait. Discarding W5 leaves us with a fairly flexible waiting shape for the final draw.  \\n\\n**Answer:** Play W5\"}"}
